# 1. BOOK IDENTITY

**Book title:** The AI-Native Engineer

**Subtitle:** Think. Build. Solve. Ship.

**Author:** Muhammad Hamid Raza (Hamid Raza)

**Book purpose:**

This book helps developers evolve beyond simply writing code. It teaches them to think clearly, understand problems, engineer software systems, work effectively with AI, build intelligent applications, solve real-world problems, and deliver meaningful outcomes.

The book covers the journey from software engineering fundamentals to modern AI-native engineering, applied AI, agentic systems, automation, cloud deployment, system design, client work, products, and startups.

The intended engineering mindset is:

- Understand before implementing.
- Think before building.
- Learn fundamentals rather than depending entirely on tools.
- Use AI as an engineering multiplier.
- Understand the systems being built.
- Build practical solutions for real problems.
- Verify what AI and software produce.
- Measure outcomes, not just lines of code.
- Deliver complete working solutions.

The book follows a practical engineering philosophy, not a hype-driven approach.

## Important terminology

AI-Native Engineer is the broad engineering direction and philosophy used by this book. It is not a universally standardized job title.

Different companies use different job titles, responsibilities, and expectations. Explain these differences honestly.

Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) is an important engineering approach covered in the book. Do not claim that every AI engineer is an FDE or that all companies use identical FDE responsibilities.

